<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="034" project="email-communication-intelligence-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Job C apply endpoint — create-task queue-feed discriminator + task fields + confirm/apply path (sibling of CommunicationProposalApplyService)</title>
    <phase>3 Pillar D — R1 carry-overs</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New BFF endpoint + new queue-feed discriminator on the audited apply/write path; caller impersonation + citation re-verify + ADR-015 no-auto-finalize. Correctness/security critical (Opus tier).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Audit + impersonation contract, ADR-015 governance, fail-closed error taxonomy; a wrong contract writes deadline-bearing task data under the wrong identity. High blast radius.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies shared Services/Communication contract (QueueFeedModels + CommunicationQueueFeedService + CommunicationEndpoints) — heavily contended with r5 (owns the renderers) + messaging/notification-spine. Execute sequentially, main-session; /conflict-check before the shared-lib/shared-service PR.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,communication,ai,audit</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-10 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add the create-task discriminator + task fields to the queue-feed contract (QueueFeedModels + CommunicationQueueFeedService) and build a Job C confirm/apply endpoint — a sibling of CommunicationProposalApplyService — that applies a confirmed kind:"create-task" proposal by calling IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync under caller impersonation, apply-time re-validation, citation re-verify, and exactly one append-only Applied audit row, failing closed with RFC-7807. Backs FR-E5.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. BFF .NET 8, Communication apply/audit path, Services/Ai/PublicContracts facade, ADR-015 data governance. Follow ADRs strictly; author literal + closed-set.</role>
  <goal>(1) QueueFeedItemKinds gains a create-task discriminator and QueueFeedItem carries the create-task fields (name/description/base-date/due-date/final-due-date/assigned-to/status/completed-date) populated for that kind; CommunicationQueueFeedService emits create-task items from the stored Job C proposals. (2) The task entity that IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync creates gains two NEW fields — `base-date` + `final-due-date` — via a dataverse-create-schema step (packed into the managed solution, ADR-027). (3) A new ICommunicationCreateTaskApplyService + POST endpoint applies a confirmed create-task proposal via **Path B (owner decision 2026-08-05)**: create the task via IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync (Subject/Description/DueDate/Regarding/Owner) under MSCRMCallerID impersonation, THEN PATCH the remaining FR-E5 fields (status/completed-date/base-date/final-due-date) via the existing caller-impersonated IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync — both writes under the SAME single append-only Applied audit row — with the same guardrails as the Job B apply sibling. The facade is UNCHANGED (ADR-013 — no new CreateTaskRequest fields, no facade widening). Registered unconditionally; publish ≤60 MB; tests added.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>FR-D5 (backs FR-E5). Job C orchestration already exists (CommunicationEnrichmentService.RunEmailCreateTaskAsync); what is missing is (a) a queue-feed kind so the Tasks reconcile tab can render create-task proposals — today QueueFeedItemKinds has only association-exception + pending-proposal — and (b) a confirm/apply endpoint that turns a confirmed proposal into a task under audit. The write core already exists: IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync (Subject/Description/DueDate/Regarding/Owner). Some FR-E5 fields (status/completed-date/base-date/final-due-date) are NOT on CreateTaskRequest; the field-mapping gap is RESOLVED as **Path B (owner decision 2026-08-05)**: create via the seam, then PATCH the remaining fields via the existing caller-impersonated IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync under the SAME append-only audit row — the facade stays unchanged (ADR-013). `base-date` + `final-due-date` are NEW fields added to the task entity via a dataverse-create-schema step in this task. The Job B apply sibling (CommunicationProposalApplyService) is the reference for the impersonation + re-validation + audit + RFC-7807 pattern.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/QueueFeedModels.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationQueueFeedService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationCreateTaskApplyService.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationProposalApplyService.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IActionSeam.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync (the blessed write core) + RunEmailCreateTaskAsync (Job C orchestration) already exist.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">SCOPE = task creation: apply ONLY via IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync (Services/Ai/PublicContracts); MUST NOT inject IOpenAiClient/IPlaybookService/node executors or synthesize a NodeExecutionContext (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">SCOPE = the apply path: nothing deadline-bearing / privilege-adjacent auto-finalizes — the task is created only on explicit human confirm; carry any privilege flag, never decide/suppress it; the final-due / deadline fields are never auto-finalized without confirmation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">SCOPE = task regarding: the created task's regarding is the confirmed association's typed record (NFR-10 — proposal actionable only after association confirmed); MUST NOT create against an unconfirmed/overridden record.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = apply guardrails (mirror the Job B sibling exactly): resolve the confirming caller server-side and fail closed 403 if unresolved; run CreateTaskAsync under MSCRMCallerID impersonation of that caller; proposal must be an OPEN pending row (409 if already resolved); re-verify the cited source text still exists against the live message (422 if not); write exactly one append-only Applied audit row (a mutate-without-audit path does not exist); all errors RFC-7807 via SdapProblemException.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">SCOPE = DI: register the new service unconditionally (Null-Object if ever feature-gated); endpoints that map unconditionally have unconditional registration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = §10 BFF hygiene: Placement Justification in PR (extends existing Services/Communication apply family in place); publish-size absolute + delta ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; add/extend tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + a seam test.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Job C confirm/apply — audited task creation via the AI facade</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-045-communication-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-004-job-contract.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="proposal-apply-sibling" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationProposalApplyService.cs">The exact 9-step apply contract to mirror: caller resolve→403, load proposal→404, pending-check→409, still-open walk→409, citation re-verify→422, apply via IActionSeam, single append-only Applied audit row, RFC-7807. Copy this shape for create-task.</pattern>
      <pattern name="public-contracts-facade" location=".claude/patterns/ai/public-contracts-facade.md">CreateTaskAsync is the blessed write core; do not bypass it.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load this POML, spec FR-D5 + FR-E5, the Job B apply sibling, IActionSeam, and QueueFeedModels. Declare RIGOR LEVEL: FULL, model-tier opus. Run /conflict-check on Services/Communication + Spaarke.Communication.Components (r5 renders the feed).</step>
    <step order="1">Extend QueueFeedItemKinds with CreateTask = "create-task" and add the create-task fields to QueueFeedItem (name/description/base-date/due-date/final-due-date/assigned-to/status/completed-date), documenting — as the record already does — which kind populates which fields; keep ranking driven by the parent communication's triage priority/RI-confidence (no second scoring scheme).</step>
    <step order="2">In CommunicationQueueFeedService, emit create-task items from the stored Job C proposals (mirror how pending-proposal items are read); do not recompute rank.</step>
    <step order="2b" name="Add task-entity schema fields (Path B)">Via dataverse-create-schema, add two NEW fields — `base-date` + `final-due-date` — to the task entity that IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync creates (`status` + `completed-date` already exist on the task entity). Pack them into the managed solution (ADR-027); do NOT widen CreateTaskRequest or the facade (ADR-013). Poll to Active; verify in the target environment.</step>
    <step order="3">Author CommunicationCreateTaskApplyService (ICommunicationCreateTaskApplyService.ApplyAsync(Guid reviewLogId/proposalId, ClaimsPrincipal? caller, ct)) mirroring the Job B sibling: caller resolve (403), load proposal (404), pending (409), still-open walk (409), citation re-verify (422), then **Path B (owner 2026-08-05)** — create via IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync mapping name→Subject / description→Description / due→DueDate / regarding→confirmed record, THEN PATCH status/completed-date/base-date/final-due-date on the created task via the caller-impersonated IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync; BOTH writes recorded under ONE append-only Applied audit row; RFC-7807 throughout.</step>
    <step order="4">Apply Path B field mapping honestly: Subject/Description/DueDate/Regarding go through IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync at create; status/completed-date/base-date/final-due-date are set by a follow-on caller-impersonated IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync PATCH on the newly-created task under the SAME audit row — do NOT silently drop a deadline-bearing field, and do NOT widen the facade (ADR-013). If the create and the PATCH cannot be bound to a single audit row, fail closed rather than writing a mutate-without-audit path.</step>
    <step order="5">Add the POST endpoint in CommunicationEndpoints.cs (sibling of /proposals/{reviewLogId}/apply), passing context.User; register the service unconditionally in CommunicationModule.cs.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests: unit tests for each fail-closed branch (unresolved caller→403, non-allow-listed/unauthorized→403, unverifiable citation→422, already-resolved→409, success→one audit row + CreateTaskAsync called under impersonation) in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/; a seam test driving the create-task queue-feed → apply happy path.</step>
    <step order="7">Build + test green; dotnet publish -c Release, record compressed size + delta; dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive.</step>
    <step order="8">Run code-review + adr-check (Step 9.5).</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="10">Document any deviation + the field-mapping decision in projects/email-communication-intelligence-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a confirmed create-task apply cannot re-verify the cited source text, fail closed with 422 (do not create the task).</trigger>
    <trigger>Path B is DECIDED (owner 2026-08-05): create via IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync, then PATCH status/completed-date/base-date/final-due-date via impersonated IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync under the same audit row; `base-date` + `final-due-date` are added as new task-entity fields (step 2b). If the task entity CANNOT accept the two new fields (schema add rejected, or UpdateRecordAsync cannot PATCH them under the caller's impersonation+single-audit-row contract), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6/§6.5 BEFORE dropping any deadline-bearing field (base-date / final-due-date / due) — silent loss of a deadline field is forbidden (ADR-015). Do NOT widen the facade (ADR-013) as a workaround.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>QueueFeedItemKinds (QueueFeedModels.cs:6) has only association-exception + pending-proposal — no create-task kind; CommunicationProposalApplyService applies Job B field-updates only, no service applies a create-task proposal (grep of Services/Communication).</existing>
    <extension>Partial — the apply service is a NEW sibling because the Job B apply is field-update-specific (allow-list re-validation + UpdateRecordAsync); it reuses the caller-resolve / citation-verify / audit helpers and the IActionSeam write core. The queue-feed kind is an additive discriminator on the EXISTING record, not a new feed.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the create-task kind + apply endpoint, the Tasks reconcile tab (FR-E5) has no proposals to render and no endpoint to POST on Approve — Job C extraction is stored-but-inert; a confirmed task proposal has nowhere to land.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish the BFF.</tool>
    <tool name="dataverse-create-schema">Add `base-date` + `final-due-date` fields to the task entity (Path B, step 2b) via Web API + PowerShell.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Models/QueueFeedModels.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationQueueFeedService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationCreateTaskApplyService.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Communication/CommunicationCreateTaskApplyServiceTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Communication/CreateTaskApplySeamTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a stored Job C proposal, when the queue-feed is read, then it emits a QueueFeedItem with Kind="create-task" carrying the task fields (name/description/base-date/due/final-due/assigned-to/status/completed), ranked by the parent communication's triage priority/RI-confidence (no second scoring scheme).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the deployed schema, when the task entity is queried, then the two NEW fields `base-date` + `final-due-date` exist and are carried in the managed solution (ADR-027).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a confirmed create-task proposal by a resolvable caller against a confirmed association, when POSTed to the apply endpoint, then (Path B) IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync is called under that caller's MSCRMCallerID impersonation AND a follow-on caller-impersonated IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync PATCHes status/completed-date/base-date/final-due-date on the created task, with BOTH writes recorded under exactly one append-only Applied audit row (no mutate-without-audit path; the facade is unchanged — no new CreateTaskRequest fields).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an unresolved caller returns 403; a proposal whose target/field is not authorized returns 403; an unverifiable citation returns 422; an already-resolved/applied proposal returns 409 — all as RFC-7807 problem responses, not unhandled errors.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Nothing deadline-bearing auto-finalizes: the task (incl. any final-due/deadline field) is created only on explicit confirm; the privilege flag is carried, never decided (ADR-015).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The service is registered unconditionally (ADR-010); publish size ≤60 MB compressed with delta reported; no new HIGH CVE; all unit + seam tests pass; build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-D5, backs FR-E5. Sibling reference = CommunicationProposalApplyService (Job B). Write core = IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync. The create-task field-mapping gap is RESOLVED as Path B (owner 2026-08-05): create via the seam, then PATCH status/completed-date/base-date/final-due-date via impersonated IActionSeam.UpdateRecordAsync under the same audit row; `base-date` + `final-due-date` added as new task-entity fields (step 2b). Facade unchanged (ADR-013; owner spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2; reach AI only via PublicContracts). Completion summary appended here when done.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
